# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        name: "Stadt St.Gallen Open Data Portal"
        url: "https://daten.stadt.sg.ch"
      }
      description: "Measures pedestrian traffic in St. Gallen, showing the number of pedestrians passing by a sensor on Vadianstrasse (at St.Galler Stadtwerke). The sensor measures pedestrians coming from the right (Neumarkt) and left (Multergasse), with hourly aggregated data. This dataset shows unprocessed live sensor data, meaning measurement errors or interruptions are not captured or corrected."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "St.Gallen Open Data API Server"
          url: "https://daten.stadt.sg.ch/api"
        }
      ]
      title: "Passantenfrequenz Stadt St.Gallen"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Hourly pedestrian counts from a sensor on Vadianstrasse in central St.Gallen"
      homepage: "https://daten.stadt.sg.ch/"
      docs_url: "https://daten.stadt.sg.ch/api"
      license_short: "Open data published by the City of St.Gallen; check the portal's terms and conditions for attribution requirements."
      license_md: `- Open data published by the [City of St.Gallen](https://daten.stadt.sg.ch/) via its open data portal
- Refer to the portal's [terms and conditions](https://daten.stadt.sg.ch/terms/terms-and-conditions/) for reuse and attribution rules
- No explicit licence string was surfaced in the catalogue page`
      about_md: `The Passantenfrequenz Stadt St.Gallen API exposes pedestrian foot-traffic counts from a sensor installed on Vadianstrasse, a street in the centre of [St.Gallen, Switzerland](https://daten.stadt.sg.ch/). The dataset is published by the City of St.Gallen on its open data portal, which is built on the [OpenDataSoft](https://www.opendatasoft.com/) platform.

What you get from the API:

- Pedestrian count records from the Vadianstrasse counter, returned newest-first
- Hourly count values that can be aggregated for daily or longer-term trends
- Standard OpenDataSoft search, facet and export operations over the dataset

The portal supports CORS for browser-based clients and exposes results through its standard records and exports endpoints. Responses are paginated; the catalogue page notes a default page size of 20 records per request.`
      entity_desc: {
        search: "Search, filter and page through pedestrian-count records from the Vadianstrasse sensor via the OpenDataSoft records endpoint exposed under the portal's `/api` base."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
